# moon_supply

Keep a Moon AE2 watchlist at target counts by exporting from Earth AE2 into the Interplanetary Railgun Sender, then firing under Earth-controller command. Moon unloads itself. Items only (no fluids).

## Non-goals

- Fluids; full AE2-Moon dump; Moon receiver control
- In-flight accounting (flight 60 s, send pause 80 s; the next poll sees Moon AE already updated)
- Legacy fire-by-full as the primary mode for this sender (use `moon_supply` earth; standalone `railgun` is manual/legacy)

## Layout

### Earth (`entries/moon_supply_E_ctrl.lua`)

- Computer on wired net + ender modem **bottom**
- `meBridge_2` on AE2-Earth; exports straight into HV loaders via `exportItemToPeripheral` (optional `buffer` chest only if leftovers exist)
- Loaders: `tfg:hv_railgun_item_loader_in_20` … `_29` (`loader_prefix`, `expected | 10`)
- `redstone_relay` **top**, pulse **`back`**
- `monitor_1` — Moon stock / phase UI

### Moon (`entries/moon_supply_M_probe.lua`)

- Computer, ender modem **top**, ME Bridge on the **right** side (`bridge | right`)
- Stock probe only: answers Earth’s `stock_req` with `getItem` counts (no local watchlist)
- Railgun receiver unloads into Moon AE without this computer

## Behaviour

1. Poll Moon stocks: Earth sends watchlist ids in `stock_req`; Moon replies `stock_res` (protocol `tfg_moon_supply`). One source of truth — Earth’s cfg.
2. Per item: `red_line = floor(target * red_frac)` (default `0.25`).
   - **ALARM** (global) if **any** item has `moon < red_line`
   - **WARN** if no ALARM but any `moon < target`
   - **OK** → idle
3. Build a shot package from deficits. Within a zone, cfg order. In **ALARM**, alarm items load before warn items of the same shot. **WARN** sends warn deficits only.
4. Missing on Earth: try `craftItem` on the **final** item (AE expands multi-step trees itself — we do not order intermediates). Prefer chunk 64→16→full→1; API success must show a real CPU job (`hasCraftJob`), else treat as fail (AP often returns true/nil with no job). `getItem.isCraftable=false` is not a hard skip. In-flight jobs + local reserve are not double-ordered. Row status: `Крафт` / `Загрузка` / `Отправлено`.
5. After the first craft probe, **unobtainable** ids are dropped from the shot. If nothing remains, **no craft-wait / no launch prep** — idle + status `не шлём (нет в AE): …`.
6. During craft-wait (**ALARM 60 s** / **WARN 120 s**, or **3 s** if no AE jobs) only for obtainable items: export AE → loaders; re-request craft as needed. Title stays short (`сборка` / `загрузка`); status lines say `крафт AE` / `сборка пакета` / `выгрузка` / `нет на Земле` — never vague «ждём AE» when nothing was ordered. Debug ring (4 lines) under the table shows snap/export/craft timings.
7. **Fire** when the obtainable shot package sits in the loaders, or when every loader is cargo-full. `загрузка` title only when loaders actually hold cargo. If the package cannot be finished after the wait, return to poll with a status note.
8. Pulse relay → `cooldown | 80`. Flight is 60 s, so the next poll sees the delivery. No in-flight reserve. A failed relay pulse does not start the cooldown.
9. **Poll UX**: one `ae_bridge.snapshot` = `getItem`×watchlist + one crafting-tasks list (never full `listItems` — that stalled large ME nets). Rows apply atomically. Shot loop refreshes staged every 0.5 s; full AE at most every 2 s. Cfg hot-reload throttled to 2 s. `requestCrafts` reuses the snapshot (no N×`craftingAmount`).

